    "theorem": "ResultantInterchangeAudit.resultant_interchange_with_degree_drop_control",
    "statement": "theorem resultant_interchange_with_degree_drop_control : (∀ (R : Type) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] (p : Polynomial R) (q : Polynomial (Polynomial R)) (r : Polynomial R) (dx dy : ℕ), q.natDegree ≤ dy → (Polynomial.Bivariate.swap q).natDegree ≤ dx → leftFixed p q r dx dy = rightFixed p q r dx dy ∧ (innerY p q dy).natDegree ≤ p.natDegree * dx ∧ (innerX q r dx).natDegree ≤ dy * r.natDegree) ∧ controlQ.natDegree = 1 ∧ (Polynomial.Bivariate.swap controlQ).natDegree = 1 ∧ (innerY controlP controlQ 1).natDegree < controlP.natDegree * 1 ∧ leftNatural controlP controlQ controlR 1 ≠ rightNatural controlP controlQ controlR 1 ∧ leftFixed controlP controlQ controlR 1 1 = rightFixed controlP controlQ controlR 1 1",
    "decl_sha256": "24ccb18a96629b4469b65e1a4626eeff74ff6682d1e45f5c28d3107aecfc93d6",
    "scope": "Fixed-size iterated Sylvester-resultant interchange over every commutative integral domain under explicit bidegree bounds, with both intermediate degree bounds derived; no nonzero/monicity/separability/characteristic/splitting/no-degree-drop premises. Actual root-multiset product/Fubini proof and injective algebraic-closure/fraction-field descent. Direct rational P=y^2-y,Q=xy+1,R=2x+1 counterexample to resetting natural outer degrees: sides -1 and2 versus fixed sides2and2, with actual bidegrees1 and strict degree drop. Separate natural-size compatibility theorem requires sharp intermediate degree equalities. Does not refute qualified Semaev or establish canonical arbitrary-split normalization, higher symmetry or higher absolute irreducibility. No native experiment or new execution assurance.",
